    README.md told a stranger that the reference deployment prints nineteen rows:
    "the fourteen above, all enabled=true". The shipped census recipe
    docs/audits/cf089-census-recipe.sh -- which tests/selftest.sh section 28 keeps in
    byte parity with that same code block -- prints nineteen rows today with
    code-factory-qa enabled=false: the scheduler auto-disabled that lane on a 90.3%
    failure rate (84/93 ticks) at 2026-11-04T03:27:07Z.
    
    The paragraph now dates the measurement, states the enabled state it actually
    observed, and says the command is the authority rather than a hand-written count.
    Wording only: the census code block is untouched, so section 28's README/mirror
    byte parity still passes.
    
