 {"id":"CF-154","title":"P4 \u2014 docs/BOARD.md's census block quotes a warning count that is not a function of the tree: two boardctl binaries print 55 vs 3 warnings for identical board bytes, and the '44 probe rows' class is gone from the current one","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-04T03:01:29Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T03:01:33Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"f31a32fd16ac90aef2cb5907312ea9cf00bc21ea8a29fd8eea06496739b1ea6d"},"reasoning":"Measured by the docs lane tick code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-02-39-16 on 2026-11-04, in the canonical checkout.\n\ndocs/BOARD.md:76-79 (section \"Current measured state\") states: \"At this tree: 116 task rows, 168 events. `scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK (47 warning(s))` \u2014 44 rows carrying a free-form `probe` key, CF-034's free-form `guard_result`/`ci_result` prose, and the headerless board (no `board.jsonl`), so header-counter checks are skipped.\"\n\nTwo independent defects in that one paragraph.\n\n(1) The counts are stale: at 472e369 the same commands give 127 task rows / 193 events (11 rows and 25 events more than the block claims) \u2014 expected drift for a block that moves with every folded row, and owned by the sync-lane census work (CF-121/CF-122).\n\n(2) The warning count is instrument-dependent, which the block does not say and cannot express. ~/.local/bin/boardctl was replaced mid-tick (mtime 2026-11-03 21:56:15 -05:00, `boardctl version` -> `dev`, no version string available). Measured, same c29c024 board bytes, two binaries:\n  - old binary: `scripts/boardctl validate` -> `RESULT: OK (55 warning(s))`, warning rows naming `key(s) {probe} outside the declared canon` for each affected task;\n  - current binary: same bytes -> `RESULT: OK (3 warning(s))`, and `grep -ci probe` on the output returns 0, although `jq -c 'select(has(\"probe\"))' .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl | wc -l` returns 53 at 472e369 (52 at c29c024).\nSo the block's explanation \"44 rows carrying a free-form `probe` key\" names a warning class the current instrument cannot emit, and every warning count already printed into docs/audits/* (47, 46, 45, 55, 3 across this week) is unreproducible without also naming the binary that produced it.\n\nThis is the doc-lane reading of the same defect class as CF-081 (hand-typed counts) and CF-121 (tautological snapshot legs): there a count was stale, here the count is not even a function of the tree alone. Filed rather than fixed because the block belongs to the sync-lane census reconciliation and a second writer would collide.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Every warning count this repository's docs quote for `boardctl validate` is accompanied by the identity of the binary that printed it (`sha256sum \"$(command -v boardctl)\"`, plus its mtime), or the count is removed from the doc in favour of the command alone.\n2. Re-runnable proof of the defect, recorded in the row's evidence artifact: one board copy, two `boardctl` binaries, two different warning totals on identical bytes (`55` vs `3` measured on 2026-11-04), with `jq 'select(has(\"probe\"))' | wc -l` showing the free-form `probe` rows still present in both runs.\n3. docs/BOARD.md's \"Current measured state\" block no longer contains the sentence \"44 rows carrying a free-form `probe` key\" unless the binary it was measured with emits that warning class \u2014 the sentence is either re-derived from the current instrument's output or deleted.\n4. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` (exit 0) at the fixed tip, and the block's own command list still reproduces byte-for-byte what the doc states about rows and events.","probe":null,"foreman_note":"Evidence artifact: docs/audits/code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-CF-129.md section 5 carries the measured matrix (same c29c024 board bytes; old binary 55 warnings with probe-canon rows, current binary 3 warnings and grep -ci probe = 0; 53 rows still carry probe at 472e369) plus the binary mtime 2026-11-03 21:56:15 -05:00