 {"id":"CF-155","title":"P4 \u2014 docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md still states 29 selftest sections while tests/selftest.sh has 30: \u00a730 landed at 1b4b0b6 and the row's own shipped drift probe exits 1 at HEAD","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":1,"created_at":"2026-11-04T03:02:01Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T03:02:01Z","detail":{"evidence":[]},"reasoning":"Measured at code-factory@c29c024 (re-verified at gh/main da84b0c). docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md states 29 numbered selftest sections twice (:7 '29 sections \u2014 plus two lettered sub-arms', :61 '`d02916e`, `tests/selftest.sh` has 29 numbered sections plus two lettered sub-arms (\u00a74b, \u00a77b)') and its reverse-direction table stops at \u00a729 (:69-96 \u2014 no \u00a730 row). tests/selftest.sh has 30: `say \"30. README Status rows 1 and 3 cite the interpreter-qualified --check\"` landed at 1b4b0b6 (2026-11-03 21:35:05, 'Addresses CF-093'), and the later c9848d7 ('docs(sync): reconcile the board census and the ACCEPTANCE-PLAN snapshot at 2c48149') re-anchored the row/event deltas while leaving the section count and the \u00a729-terminated table untouched. The instrument CF-099 shipped for exactly this drift (docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh) therefore exits 1 at HEAD with 'DRIFT: plan says 29 sections, tests/selftest.sh has 30'. Nothing forces a new numbered section to update the plan: no selftest arm reads docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md, so the gate stays green (SELFTEST: PASS at c29c024) while the plan describes a tree that no longer exists. DISTINCT FROM CF-113 (the census regex cannot see LETTERED sub-arms, \u00a77b) and CF-121 (the probe's snapshot leg is a tautology) and CF-115 (legs the probe certifies without measuring): this is a NUMBERED section the census sees, dropped by the plan side, and the probe's own measured leg is what reds. CF-099 is complete and was correct at its own closure commit a9d0cc8; the rot arrived later with 1b4b0b6, so this is fresh drift, not a reopen. ch:trace row=CF-154 spe