 {"id":"CF-156","title":"P2 \u2014 an unresolved secret-scanning alert sits open on the PUBLIC repo: a slack-token-shaped fixture is still reachable at commit 8edba9f and nothing in the fleet triages alerts","status":"complete","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-04T03:25:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T03:45:11Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"17632956f9c494c25d2914e6cceaaa9b1323498a2aaf524d77901ff58d6d4cdb","evidence":[{"run_id":"783e56f0","ts":"2026-11-04T03:45:11Z","tree_fp":"fee51a3742f0d2b254bef27cb24eb1bb2ae082076f9b9e1d6ac326bc47463429","artifacts":[".gitreins/history/2026-11-04/783e56f0/verdict.json"]}]},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-04 on a fresh clone of origin/main (dae4e7a) with gh: `repos/coding-hermes/code-factory/secret-scanning/alerts?state=open` returns exactly 1 alert and `?state=resolved` returns 0. Alert 1 has been OPEN since 2026-11-02T11:22:58Z \u2014 across at least six releng/readme/qa ticks \u2014 with secret_type `slack_api_token`, provider Slack, `validity: unknown`, and `publicly_leaked: true`, on a repository whose visibility is PUBLIC. Nothing has ever resolved or dismissed an alert in this repo.\n\nThe reported location is `.hermes/scripts/test_secret_scrub.py:30` at commit 8edba9f (\"fix(security): SEC-001 write-time secret scrub for chat-archive ingestion\"), blob 7d38bc75d6071de0ad2f3c4344cc128fd668df0d. That path is ABSENT from the current tree (`git ls-files --error-unmatch` fails), so the alert is historical rather than live-tree: the blob is still reachable from public history (`git cat-file -e 8edba9f` succeeds). The value is a scrubber test fixture \u2014 its neighbours in the same table are documented placeholders (AWS's own public example access-key id, the sha1/sha256 of the empty string, `Sup3rFakePassw0rd`) \u2014 so rotation is probably not the remedy. But \"probably a fixture\" is a judgement someone has to RECORD, not a state the repo can keep ignoring: a scraped Slack token with `validity: unknown` is the class of finding a public repo is expected to close out.\n\nThe posture asymmetry is the actual defect. Secret scanning AND push protection are enabled (`security_and_analysis.secret_scanning.status=enabled`, `secret_scanning_push_protection.status=enabled`), so a new push of that shape is blocked at the door \u2014 yet there is no triage loop behind the alert: 0 resolved, 0 dismissed, no owner, no board row until this one. Push protection also means the repository's own fixture must be documented so a future editor understands why the shape is there and does not \"fix\" it by rotating something fictional.\n\nNot filed as a duplicate: CF-120 records the protection SETTINGS (secret scanning on, branch protection absent) but says nothing about the one open alert; CF-050/CF-086 cover absolute host paths, not credential shapes. This row is the alert's triage and the fixture's documentation, and it is P2 because it is an unresolved leaked-shaped credential in public history rather than a wording defect.","acceptance_criteria":"1. `gh api 'repos/coding-hermes/code-factory/secret-scanning/alerts?state=open' --jq 'length'` prints 0, with EITHER a dismissal carrying a resolution comment that names the fixture file and the commit it came from, OR \u2014 if the owner rules the value real \u2014 a recorded rotation plus the history remedy the owner chose. A silent `state=open` count of 0 achieved by deleting the alert is not acceptance.\n2. The in-tree fixture stops re-tripping the provider detector: the file that carries the slack-shaped fixture (or its successor) documents with a comment that the value is a scrubber fixture and names the GitHub alert it once raised, and a commit touching that file produces no NEW alert (`gh api 'repos/coding-hermes/code-factory/secret-scanning/alerts' --jq 'length'` unchanged).\n3. The row records who triaged it and the reason code used, so the next releng tick can re-measure criterion 1 without re-deciding the question.\n4. The remedy introduces no new absolute host paths, credentials, or internal endpoints: `git grep -nE 'xox[bprs]-' -- . | grep -v <the documented fixture path>` is empty and the tree's ruff/selftest gates still pass (`bash tests/selftest.sh` -> `SELFTEST: PASS`).","probe":null,"commit_hash":"f54c54b5c8bd94e603f6419f90cbbe5b96e27ae6","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":"Alert 1 dismissed as used_in_tests with a comment naming .hermes/scripts/test_secret_scrub.py line 30 at commit 8edba9f; docs/SECURITY-TRIAGE.md records the triage and the re-measure commands. Verified: alerts?state=open length 0, alerts/1 resolution used_in_tests, selftest PASS at f54c54b, tier2 verdict 1fd1b009 PASS."}
